Humm.. the end-game doesn't necessarily begin from the first entrance
through the magic portal.
For example, I usually make a short visit there when I check which one of
the two fakewiz levels has the portal. 

And in the game I ascended last Sunday, I ended up spending quite some
time there that time.. there was an arch-lich that decided to begin a
summon storm right there and then. One of the creatures summoned was a
balrog that yanked Mjollnir from my hands with its bullwhip. Before I had
killed all the bad guys there, my Hp got so low that I considered it too
dangerous to use one more turn doing ANYTHING else but break a wand of
teleport to get some space between them and myself.
Of course, Mjollnir also got teleported. Luckily I also had +6 Excalibur,
so I was not rendered weaponless, but I still wanted to get Mjollnir back.
When I had killed all the summoned nasties and the arch-lich itself, 
I didn't find Mjollnir in that room. I cleared the whole bottom floor of
the Wizard's house, but no Mojo to be found.
I went out and climbed back to search the rest of the level, THINKING I
was checking every square, but still didn't find it.
Well, let's go on with Excalibur, I thought.. and mapped out the rest of
Gehennom and found the vibrating square.
Then I remembered I didn't have the Candelabrum yet, so I went to Vlad's
tower, cleared it and got the thing. Then I remembered I didn't have the
necessary amount of candles yet, carried the Candelabrum and the Bell to
the stairs of the VS level and went on my way back to Minetown to buy 5
more candles (I had found two elsewhere).
And when I was crossing the level with the bottom floor of Rodney's house,
THEN I suddenly found Mjollnir on the floor on a square I THOUGHT I had
checked earlier :-)

Well, that game was my first actual wishless ascension. Also polyselfless,
polyitemless and genocideless, but not my first ascension with those
conducts.
Once earlier I have had an ALMOST wishless ascension, but accidentally hit
a wrong inventory letter when I mean to zap some other wand on dungeon
level 1 with the Amulet. I don't remember whether that was with a version
before wishing for "nothing" was added, or forgot to wish for nothing, or
did I just think of something I liked to have.

Anyway, I had a lot of action between going through Rodney's portal the
first time and actually starting my final end-game run.

